course: dictionary
lesson: 6433
title: Mystery, a word with many doors
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mystery is something strange that is not known or explained yet. «Scratching and creaking at night» is a mystery until you find the cause, such as mice, branches or wind. Read the words around the word to check: is something unknown, or is someone trying to solve it?
explain: Mystery can also mean a story or film where a detective solves a crime or a puzzle. «Solve the mystery» and «murder mystery» both point to this meaning. A detective often works from clues, just as you do when you use context.
explain: As a special kind of word, «mystery» can work like an adjective, describing something you do not know yet. «A mystery prize» is one you will only find out about when it opens. In maths, a «mystery number» is the unknown number you must find.
fact: Mystery is a noun, with the plural mysteries.
fact: «Mystery» means something strange that is not known or explained yet.
fact: «Mystery» can also mean a story or film about solving a crime or puzzle, often by a detective.
fact: In maths, a «mystery number» is the number you have to find, often by doing the opposite operation.
fact: Scientists still try to solve mysteries, such as what is at the bottom of the ocean.
exercise: «Scratching and creaking at night» is a mystery until you find the cause. What is a mystery? | *Something strange that is not known or explained yet | A loud noise that always has a clear answer | A type of pet mouse
exercise: In maths, what is a «mystery number»? | *A number you have to find | A number that has been written twice | A number that is always odd | A number you already know
exercise: Which of these is a story where a detective solves a crime? | A mystery number | A mystery prize | A loot box | *A murder mystery
test: The Mock Turtle's joke «Mystery (history)» is a sound-alike joke. Which subject does it play on? | Maths | Drawing | *History | Geography
test: «A loot box is a paid mystery prize in a game.» What is a mystery prize? | A type of detective | *A prize you do not know about until it opens | A rule book for the game | A free map of the game
exam: Which meaning fits «solve the mystery» in a detective story? | A happy surprise party | A type of spelling test | A kind of weather | *Something unknown that a detective works to explain
